where `F` charges captured leaves, and `G` charges the pending operands’ captures other than `x`. Thus a minimum source either has an occurrence of `x` in `E`, or satisfies the corresponding nonnegative-charge inequality. See [minimum_nested_alternative](/Users/a9lim/Work/blam/tmp/round4/close46/NestedLets.lean:243).

